  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cultural traditions and income generation in the Quilombo Morro Seco</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Associao Quilombola So Miguel Arcanjo do Bairro Morro Seco (AQSMA), $45,315 over 18 months AQSMA will work with residents of a quilombo in the state of Sao Paulo to preserve traditional agro-ecological practices, create a seed bank, develop the connection between young people and the land, help families use cultural events to generate income and improve its own ability to manage future grants. The project should benefit 50 residents of Morro Seco directly and 90 indirectly. 18</narrative>
  </description>
